WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.530
In 1958, the economist A.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:07.990
W. Phillips plotted British
data from 1861 to 1957.

3
00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.880
When unemployment was low,
money wages rose fast.

4
00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.420
When it was high, they rose slowly.

5
00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:16.650
To many, it looked like a menu.

6
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.930
Governments could choose a point on it.

7
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.390
So can a country buy lower
unemployment by accepting

8
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.190
a little more inflation?

9
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:28.310
In this mission, you'll link that
curve to aggregate demand and supply,

10
00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:29.980
frame by frame.

11
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:31.830
Then you'll use a graph lab:

12
00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:35.750
slide unemployment down and
see what happens to inflation.

13
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:38.870
Your mission: find out
whether that deal is real,

14
00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:40.200
and whether it lasts.
